# TASK: Implement Real AWS Cloud Connection Module for CloudOps

We need to implement the real AWS cloud-account connection flow in CloudOps.

IMPORTANT:
This is NOT a UI-only task.

Implement the complete backend + security/session layer + frontend connection modal + database integration required for a real AWS connection.

The target UX is the AWS connection modal shown in the provided reference.

The target authentication flow is:

User
  ↓
CloudOps AWS Connection Modal
  ↓
AWS Region
AWS Access Key ID
AWS Secret Access Key
AWS Session Token (optional)
Assume Role ARN (optional)
  ↓
CloudOps Backend
  ↓
Validate AWS credentials
  ↓
AWS STS GetCallerIdentity
  ↓
Optional STS AssumeRole
  ↓
Temporary AWS session
  ↓
Persist ONLY safe cloud-account metadata
  ↓
Connected AWS Account
  ↓
CloudOps Tool Gateway can later use the temporary session
  ↓
AWS APIs

DO NOT expose AWS credentials to agents.

DO NOT store AWS secret credentials in PostgreSQL.

DO NOT store AWS credentials in browser storage.

DO NOT log credentials.

