3. API CONTRACT
============================================================

Implement:

POST /v1/cloud-accounts

Protected by the existing operator authentication mechanism.

Use tenant isolation.

Request body:

{
  "provider": "aws",
  "region": "us-east-1",
  "accessKeyId": "...",
  "secretAccessKey": "...",
  "sessionToken": "...",
  "assumeRoleArn": "..."
}

Rules:

- provider must be "aws"
- region must be valid
- accessKeyId required
- secretAccessKey required
- sessionToken optional
- assumeRoleArn optional

Do NOT return credentials in the response.

Response should contain only safe account metadata.

Example:

{
  "id": "cld_...",
  "provider": "aws",
  "accountId": "123456789012",
  "region": "us-east-1",
  "roleArn": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/CloudOpsRole",
  "status": "CONNECTED"
}

Only return fields that actually exist in the implementation.

