============================================================
5. INITIAL AWS CREDENTIAL VALIDATION
============================================================

When POST /v1/cloud-accounts is received:

1. Validate request schema.
2. Validate operator authentication.
3. Validate tenant.
4. Validate AWS credentials.
5. Create an AWS STS client using the supplied credentials.
6. Call:

GetCallerIdentity

This proves that the supplied AWS credentials are valid.

Extract:

AWS Account ID
Caller ARN
Caller User/Role identity where appropriate

Do not trust an account ID supplied by the frontend.

The account ID must come from AWS.

============================================================
6. OPTIONAL ASSUME ROLE
============================================================

If Assume Role ARN is provided:

After validating the supplied credentials with
GetCallerIdentity:

Call:

STS AssumeRole

using:

RoleArn = supplied Assume Role ARN

RoleSessionName = generated CloudOps session identifier

SessionDuration = short-lived value within AWS limits.

Prefer a short duration appropriate for CloudOps operations.

Do not use unnecessarily long-lived temporary credentials.

If AssumeRole succeeds:

Use the resulting temporary credentials for the CloudOps
AWS session.

If AssumeRole fails:

Return a safe error.

Do not persist the cloud account as connected.

Do not expose STS credentials to the browser.

============================================================
