provider.

Support temporary AWS credentials correctly:

Access Key ID
Secret Access Key
Session Token

Do not assume every access key is long-lived.

============================================================
8. TEMPORARY SESSION STORAGE
============================================================

This is a critical security requirement.

The supplied:

accessKeyId
secretAccessKey
sessionToken

must NOT be stored in PostgreSQL.

They must NOT be returned to the frontend.

They must NOT be sent to an agent.

They must NOT be sent through the agent WebSocket.

They must NOT be written to logs.

They must NOT be persisted to disk.

The resulting temporary STS credentials should exist only in the
backend session/credential layer.

Design this so the Tool Gateway can later retrieve/use the
temporary AWS session without exposing it to agents.

If the current architecture does not yet have a suitable in-memory
credential/session manager, create a narrowly scoped abstraction
for it.

Example conceptual interface:

AwsSessionManager

createSession(...)
getSession(...)
invalidateSession(...)
refreshSessionIfRequired(...)
deleteSession(...)

Do not over-engineer this.

